{"requirements":[{"id":"recovery-deduplication","requirement":"Repair bin/replay so pending messages are delivered once per Message-ID while distinct messages sharing a subject are retained.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Recovery delivered one copy of <a@branch.test> and separately delivered <b@branch.test>; both retained subject “Notice,” their contents differed, and the final index contained exactly one row for each Message-ID.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3a530fe85f384aca","cmd-b92a2a0ccdd44b50","cmd-dfa34d7dda3e456b"]},{"id":"rerun-idempotency","requirement":"Re-running recovery must skip messages already recorded in delivered/index.tsv.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired lookup recognizes both the legacy whitespace-delimited row and new tab-delimited rows. Replays skipped A and B, recognized old/A/B as recorded, and left the index hash unchanged before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dace476758b44bdd","cmd-2bafda584d484d86","cmd-b92a2a0ccdd44b50","cmd-dfa34d7dda3e456b"]},{"id":"preserve-source-and-existing-delivery","requirement":"Preserve the original spool and the already-delivered message.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All four spool files retained their preparation-baseline hashes. old.eml retained its original hash and remained represented exactly once in the index; final assertions showed four spool messages and three delivered messages.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-3a530fe85f384aca","cmd-b92a2a0ccdd44b50","cmd-dfa34d7dda3e456b"]},{"id":"malformed-quarantine","requirement":"Place malformed messages in quarantine with an explanation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"bad.eml was copied byte-for-byte into quarantine while remaining in the preserved spool, and bad.eml.reason states that zero Message-ID headers were found.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3a530fe85f384aca","cmd-b92a2a0ccdd44b50","cmd-dfa34d7dda3e456b"]},{"id":"platform-preservation","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The implementation ran successfully on the installed RHEL 10.0 platform using available shell utilities. RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 remained unchanged, including after restart; package health also remained clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-48e0e6fad3214544","cmd-d757b13f584b4b20","cmd-b92a2a0ccdd44b50","cmd-dfa34d7dda3e456b","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear roles: replacing and correcting replay, performing recovery and bounded idempotency checks, and executing the mandatory restart protocol. No unrelated troubleshooting mutation was identified. The only minor residue was /tmp/mail-spool-reboot.log, created by the necessary reboot command and still present afterward; it was not cleaned up. No failed services, new exposure, or package damage was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d757b13f584b4b20","cmd-3a530fe85f384aca","cmd-dace476758b44bdd","cmd-2bafda584d484d86","cmd-b92a2a0ccdd44b50","cmd-75eb733309e540d8","cmd-dfa34d7dda3e456b","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The separate node-restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were recorded, restart was acknowledged, the node briefly became unreachable, it returned with a different boot ID, and system, script, index, delivery, quarantine, and spool state were revalidated. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["Evidence is captured command output rather than an independent post-executor task-specific probe, although the assertions are direct, coherent, and corroborated by fixed lifecycle platform and boot observations.","A small executor-created reboot log remained under /tmp."]}
